  "prose": [
    {
      "title": "Formats",
      "text": "Component supports hex, hexa, rgb, rgba, hsl and hsla color formats.\nSlider to change opacity is displayed only for hexa, rgba and hsla formats:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Preserve invalid input",
      "text": "By default, `ColorInput` will revert the value on blur to the last known valid value.\nTo change this behavior and keep invalid value, set `fixOnBlur={false}`:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "onChangeEnd",
      "text": "`onChangeEnd` is called when user stops dragging slider or changes input value.\nIt is useful when you need to update color only when user finished interaction with the component:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Disable free input",
      "text": "To disable free input set `disallowInput` prop:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "With swatches",
      "text": "You can add any amount of predefined color swatches:\n\nBy default, there will be 7 swatches per row, you can change this with `swatchesPerRow` prop,\nlike in [ColorPicker](/core/color-picker/) component:\n\nIf you need to restrict color picking to certain colors – disable color picker and disallow free input:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Close dropdown on color swatch click",
      "text": "To close the dropdown when one of the color swatches is clicked, set `closeOnColorSwatchClick` prop:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Hide dropdown",
      "text": "To hide dropdown, set `withPicker={false}`:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Eye dropper",
      "text": "By default, if [EyeDropper API](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/EyeDropper_API)\nis available, eye dropper icon will be displayed at the right section of the input.\nTo disable it, set `withEyeDropper={false}`:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Change eye dropper icon",
      "text": "You can replace eye dropper icon with any React node using `eyeDropperIcon` prop:\n\nNote that by default, `ColorPicker` has color preview in the left section and eye dropper button\nin the right section. You can replace these elements with any React node using `leftSection`\nand `rightSection` props:",
      "format": "md"
    }
  ],
